# What `vercel deploy` uploads from this folder: only what web/ needs to build (the web
# app, the contract it imports, and the workspace manifests npm ci checks), plus the
# project config in vercel.json. Everything else, .env above all, stays on this machine.
#
# vercel.json lives here rather than in web/ because the upload root is this folder: the
# workspace build needs packages/contract. Vercel reads the root vercel.json, not
# web/vercel.json, so the root file repeats web's SPA fallback; /evals loads on a direct hit.
/*
!/vercel.json
!/web
!/packages
!/backend
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/tsconfig.base.json
/backend/*/*
!/backend/*/package.json
**/node_modules
**/dist
